<section class="wrap section section--flush" id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
      <h2 id="problem-title">AI agents can now read what your organisation publishes</h2>
      <ul class="quotes quotes--solo"><li><figure><blockquote><p>It's about what an AI agent can discover from the public internet.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="cite"><strong>Bluebird AI Solutions</strong></figcaption></figure></li></ul>
    </div>
    <div class="copy">
      <p>Risk used to sit mainly behind the firewall. AI agents can now discover, read and connect what your organisation has already published on the public internet.</p>
      <p>Over time, websites collect documents, pages and settings that reveal more than anyone intended: staff details in a published PDF, an internal report that a search engine has indexed, software versions in page headers. An AI agent can find and connect items like these quickly.</p>
      <p>Organisations need to see their sites the way an AI agent does, and then fix what that view exposes.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

